        {
          "id": 1209397837,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The issue here is the complete different expectation of the user with a well-established feature. From a UI perspective it would make more sense to differentiate the origin of the drag/drop or right-mouse-click operation. If it starts above the field name, than only drop the field. If it starts above the value, drop everything.\n\nI agree with the Ctrl thing being not shown to many users. Coincidentally Ctrl might not be a good idea, as - I think - it is already in use to create a \"Prepare as \" drop instead of an \"Apply as \" drop.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
